WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.970
Over the past several years, many of us have
learned how incredibly life-threatening and

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:08.090
dangerous viruses and diseases can be.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.110
They can cause any number of critical symptoms
and can shut down your body’s processes

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.390
in a wide variety of ways.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:18.750
But there are more diseases than just the
ones we can name off the top of our heads

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.920
based on our recent experience.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.279
Many of these have nothing anomalous about
them, despite being incredibly strange.

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:30.119
Take progeria: it’s a genetic condition
that causes people carrying a very specific

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:32.640
gene mutation to age rapidly.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.320
Not twice as fast, either - so fast that most
victims tragically don’t live past their

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.320
early teens.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.430
Or elephantiasis.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.220
If you’re thinking that’s a disease affecting
elephants, you’d be wrong, but not grossly

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.220
so.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.560
It causes the lymph nodes in your body to
stop draining fluid correctly, so it pools

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.780
up and makes your body parts swell to a massive
size - until you look like an elephant.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.960
And of course, there’s the nasty disease
known more commonly as the bone-growth disease,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.010
or the bone-prison syndrome.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:07.799
When most people’s muscle cells die, they
get a nasty bruise but no lasting damage.

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:13.840
But for people with this rare genetic mutation,
dead muscle cells ossify - they turn into

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.840
bone.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.060
And muscle cells die slowly anyway, even if
they’re not damaged in any way.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.679
Over the years, sufferers have their body
gradually turn into solid bone.

00:01:23.679 --> 00:01:25.869
All strange and terrifying, aren’t they?

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:29.509
But none of them are anomalies, surprising
as it may seem.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:34.439
They’re all perfectly real diseases, documented
by modern science - you can even search them

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:37.149
up and see evidence, if you don’t believe
us.

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:42.009
But it begs the question: if these seemingly
logic-defying and impossible diseases are

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:46.969
just the ones known by modern science, then
what kind of diseases break our understanding

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:52.939
of science, physics, biology, and chemistry
so much that they need to be categorized as

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:53.939
anomalous?

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:57.029
And, of course, contained by the Foundation.

00:01:57.029 --> 00:02:03.840
We have a few examples: the most notable of
which is SCP-008, the fabled “Zombie Plague”.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.749
Exactly what it sounds like on the tin.

00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:10.470
But today we’re going to be looking at something
else entirely: one of the many “anomalous

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:14.260
biohazards” that the Foundation keeps in
cold-storage deep below the surface of the

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.569
Earth to ensure that they never infect another
human being again.

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:23.569
But this one is a little unique - when we
talk about dangerous diseases, we always consider

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:28.209
the outcome, the most danger a disease could
possibly pose, to be death.

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:30.879
However, our topic for the day doesn’t do
that.

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:34.680
Frankly, death might be preferable to what
it does to you.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.250
SCP-2376 has a nickname around the Foundation’s
medical department.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.760
They call it “the Scarecrow Virus”.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.409
That name alone raises a lot of questions
- usually diseases are named scientifically,

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:50.720
or according to the symptoms they give to
anyone unlucky enough to be infected by them.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.190
But scarecrows aren’t dangerous - they’re
not even alive.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.959
The simple little straw effigies that farmers
stick in their corn and wheat fields so that

00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:01.629
crows don’t pick their crops clean before
they can even be harvested.

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:06.180
What do scarecrows have to do with a biological
threat that the Foundation has decided is

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:11.280
dangerous and anomalous enough that it must
be contained, lest the wider world learn about

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.280
it?

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:16.840
Well, I suppose the only way to find out is
by reading its documentation.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.060
Which is, honestly, quite sparse.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.950
It’s not the massive multi-page goliaths
that many entries can turn into - it’s short,

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.170
it’s simple, and perhaps it's better that
way.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:31.230
This is one of those cases where the more
details you get, the more disturbing the anomaly

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.230
is.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.159
But let’s get into it.

00:03:34.159 --> 00:03:37.069
SCP-2376’s object class is euclid.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:39.090
Which is, at least, a good first sign.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:44.090
It means that it’s not too hard to contain,
which in the context of a disease means that

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.209
it’s not amazingly communicative or contagious.

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:55.560
That’s good, all things considered - SCP-008
and SCP-610, by contrast, are incredibly communicative

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.629
and that’s part of why they can be so hard
for the Foundation to contain.

00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:05.409
The Special Containment Procedures for SCP-2376
are a little odd - in fact, they barely reference

00:04:05.409 --> 00:04:07.380
SCP-2376 itself.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:13.200
Instead, they mostly refer to SCP-2376-1 instances.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.889
And how to care for them, feed them, communicate
with them, and so on and so forth.

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:24.580
They go into detail that SCP-2376-1 instances
can’t be fed normally, but by using an automated

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.690
feeding system to limit human exposure to
them.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:32.300
But they still need meticulous care - they
have to be examined at least once every 8

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.290
hours by Foundation medical staff - and the
discomfort that comes as a result of their

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.389
infections is to be alleviated as much as
possible.

00:04:39.389 --> 00:04:42.630
While precise, they’re not exactly surprising.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:48.580
We know it’s a disease, so it makes sense
that these SCP-2376-1 instances are the victims

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.400
of the disease - and as they’re severely
ill, they need to be fed and examined without

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.340
making their condition, whatever it is, even
worse or spreading it to staff.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.940
But they go on, and they get stranger.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.479
SCP-2376-1 instances can’t actually be informed
or made aware of the fact that the disease

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:12.669
they’re suffering from, SCP-2376, is anomalous
for some reason.

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:15.490
They can’t be told about the anomalous properties
of it.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.580
A text-based communicator for the disabled,
kind of like the computer-voice system used

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:24.800
by Stephen Hawking, has to be used to communicate
with the instances, but personnel can’t

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.720
just wait for them to type something out.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.410
They have to close and reopen their eyes every
5 minutes to see if they’ve typed anything

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.410
out.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:37.199
For some reason, either victims of SCP-2376
can’t move when they’re being looked at,

00:05:37.199 --> 00:05:42.360
like the infamous SCP-173, or that people
can’t sense that victims have moved until

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.460
they close and reopen their eyes.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:49.729
Either way, very anomalous, not to mention
the fact that they won’t or can’t speak.

00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:55.690
The next line is a very hard, very firm rule,
though, not just a directive for care: “Under

00:05:55.690 --> 00:06:01.240
absolutely no circumstances are patients to
be removed from their rooms or disposed of”.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:05.710
No removing from rooms makes sense - you don’t
want the disease to spread and cross-contaminate

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.680
with the various other anomalies that a Foundation
site has in its halls.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.400
Who knows what kind of superbug you might
wind up with?

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.979
But ‘disposal’ is a different matter - the
Foundation isn’t allowed to get rid of victims

00:06:16.979 --> 00:06:18.550
of this disease.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:22.800
That seems obvious - the Foundation doesn’t
kill people if at all avoidable.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.470
Clearly, something else is at play here.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.620
The next line gives a hint: personnel have
to follow any instructions given to them while

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:36.389
treating instances, and have to be regularly
reminded that they’re treating a human being.

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:41.260
Whatever this disease does to people, it causes
others to not recognize them as human and

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.430
may accidentally dispose of them.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:49.860
All the instances/victims, as well as samples
of the disease itself, are located at Site-234

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.490
and MTF Beta-7, the “Maz Hatters”
are to regularly investigate hospitals in

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:57.650
areas with prior infection for repeat instances.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:02.349
Beta-7 is a Mobile Task Force trained and
equipped specifically to deal with contagious

00:07:02.349 --> 00:07:06.990
or infectious anomalies, a cross between soldiers
and doctors.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:14.159
SCP-2376 is a substrain of the real-world
tetanus virus, which is often called lockjaw.

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:18.051
Most people get a tetanus shot in childhood
that protects them from the disease, with

00:07:18.051 --> 00:07:22.410
regular booster shots, so they never have
to suffer through the grisly infection that’s

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.580
often found on rusty metal.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:29.569
Lockjaw is called that because the bacteria
infects your muscles and makes them violently

00:07:29.569 --> 00:07:33.400
spasm, locking your jaw muscles into a closed
position.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.400
There’s no cure, and about ten percent of
cases are fatal.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.370
But the Scarecrow Virus is different.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:46.740
While tetanus is found on rusty nails, SCP-2376
is zoonotic; it’s communicated and carried

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.120
by animals, specifically the common crow.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.759
That sheds some light on the name.

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:55.410
While it’s carried by crows, it’s transmissible
to humans too.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:08:03.700
As we guessed, the unfortunate victims are
designated SCP-2376-1 instances by the Foundation.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:09.949
SCP-2376’s infection of humans consists
of two distinct stages, Stage 1 and Stage

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:10.949
2.

00:08:10.949 --> 00:08:14.080
Stage 1 is, of course, first, and at first
seems mild.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:19.259
It lasts between one and four weeks and has
all the symptoms of the regular tetanus virus,

00:08:19.259 --> 00:08:25.050
like a fever, spasms, and loss of mobility,
but with some extra ones - people also develop

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:30.949
a reddish rash across their body, a cough,
and vertigo; they become afraid of heights.

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:34.490
That would be strange enough, but it also
affects the senses.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:38.060
Victims who haven’t progressed to Stage
2 yet complain about always smelling the odor

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:42.690
of straw, corn, and other materials you’d
find on a farm, even when they’re nowhere

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.190
near any farm.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:49.010
They say that everything they touch has a
strange sort of film or texture on it, like

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:53.380
rough burlap - the kind you’d find a bag
of potatoes to be made of.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:57.740
This is all certainly strange, but it’s
not something that you’d think MUST be contained

00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.260
by the Foundation.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.610
Just an odd variant of the tetanus virus.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:04.730
But Stage 2 is where things really get complicated.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.870
The anomalous properties of the disease become
readily apparent after the victim progresses

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:10.540
to Stage 2.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:15.680
They stop being perceived as human - anyone
who looks at them only sees a regular, unmoving,

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.250
inanimate scarecrow.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:20.130
It’s not that they become a scarecrow, either.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:25.590
Just that people can no longer perceive them
as anything but - which is arguably worse.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:29.730
Observers don’t realize that the person
they were looking at just a moment ago is

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:34.899
suddenly gone or has been replaced by a scarecrow
- to them, everything seems normal.

00:09:34.899 --> 00:09:36.912
They don’t realize or question that anything’s
wrong.

00:09:36.912 --> 00:09:45.420
In fact, they can’t even perceive any noises
a SCP-2376-1 instance makes, like yelling

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.770
or calling for help.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.910
That’s why they have to use the text communicators.

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.060
But why the five minute delay?

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:57.620
Because people can’t perceive any motion
by SCP-2376-1 instances either, at least not

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.050
while looking at them.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:03.480
If one runs across the room right in front
of an observer, they won’t realize it, and

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.310
will see the scarecrow still sitting where
it started.

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:11.060
But, if they look away by turning around or
closing their eyes before making visual contact

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:17.680
with it again, the scarecrow will be in the
position where the SCP-2376-1 instance stopped

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:18.680
moving.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:23.470
The disease doesn’t just affect the person
who has it - once Stage 2 sets in, it affects

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:28.240
people who don’t have it and have no exposure
to it, besides looking at a victim.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:33.680
That’s why it’s anomalous - it manages
to change how people’s nervous systems and

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:37.220
senses act while never even infecting them.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:42.470
SCP-2376 can’t infect microphones or motion
detectors either, though.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:47.050
Any sounds made will still be picked up in
a sound recording, and anyone tripping a motion

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:49.640
detector alarm will have it sound immediately.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.990
That makes containment a little easier, now
that the Foundation can depend on at least

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.500
physics and sound.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:01.080
But then you’d think a picture or photograph
of an SCP-2376-1 instance would look like

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.750
a normal person, right?

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:06.339
Albeit bedridden with a rash and spasming,
but a human being.

00:11:06.339 --> 00:11:09.689
You’d be wrong, and same about videos.

00:11:09.689 --> 00:11:15.410
Visual media just renders victims as what
they appear to the naked eye: a regular, harmless

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.410
scarecrow.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:21.889
There is one way to stop the effect that SCP-2376
has on perceiving its victims - but it’s

00:11:21.889 --> 00:11:22.889
not pretty.

00:11:22.889 --> 00:11:27.171
When a victim dies of the infection, they
can be perceived as a human again, though

00:11:27.171 --> 00:11:30.370
of course by then it’s far too late.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:35.070
Thankfully, being infected by SCP-2376 isn’t
a death sentence.

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:39.220
The parts and symptoms of the disease that
are shared with regular tetanus can be alleviated

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.920
with the same treatments and remedies - though
they can’t be fully cured.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:48.510
And even if all the other symptoms go away,
the largest and most anomalous aspect, the

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:51.090
effect on others perceptions, stays.

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:55.899
As of testing so far, there’s no way to
get rid of that aspect of the disease - except,

00:11:55.899 --> 00:11:57.300
of course, death.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:02.980
And the Foundation has performed extensive
testing with samples of SCP-2376.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.980
Murine models - they infected lab rats with
the disease to see if the reaction was the

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:10.690
same as humans and how it compared to lab
rats with tetanus.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:17.470
The answer was extremely similar: just like
tetanus, if a SCP-2376-1 instance was pregnant

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:21.560
when they were infected, the disease would
easily transfer to the fetus and give the

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:23.779
baby the Scarecrow Virus from birth.

00:12:23.779 --> 00:12:29.120
And rats that went to Stage 2 also were perceived
as scarecrows - tiny little straw-stuffed

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:33.149
scarecrows shaped like mice and stuffed with
denim and straw.

00:12:33.149 --> 00:12:36.820
But unlike humans, rats and mice eat straw.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:41.310
Which is exactly what the non-infected rats
began to do to the infected ones.

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:47.360
They were unable to perceive the rat’s cries
or thrashing, and cannibalized it - but SCP-2376

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.990
and tetanus are bacterial infections.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:54.560
By eating the infected rats, the other rats
also became infected, showing the disturbed

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:58.800
Foundation researchers how this disease managed
to spread unnoticed.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.570
Protocols were immediately implemented to
make sure rats and mice couldn’t get into

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:09.180
the containment chambers of SCP-2376-1 instances,
lest they try to start eating them and spread

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.670
the disease like wildfire through Site-234.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:18.200
Until the medical researchers can get a better
understanding of what exactly SCP-2376 is

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:24.160
and how it affects other animals besides crows,
people, and mice, testing is ordered to continue

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:28.150
and several other researchers have noted how
similar the effects of the virus are to other

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:35.070
anomalies, such as SCP-2316, a pathogen that
causes the entire body to lock up and stop

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:41.840
doing everything, and SCP-2218, a number of
teleporting intelligent scarecrows.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:47.649
Maybe SCP-2376 is the result of these two
anomalies coming into contact and interacting,

00:13:47.649 --> 00:13:50.060
as some of the researchers are investigating?

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:55.769
Or maybe it’s much more nefarious - perhaps
these three anomalies share a common, synthetic

00:13:55.769 --> 00:14:00.060
origin, like someone trying to create an anomalous
biological weapon.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.220
Or maybe it really just is a coincidence.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:08.800
SCP-2376 was first encountered by the Foundation
in the exact place anyone would expect to

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:14.709
find straw and scarecrows: the wide, vast
cornfields of Iowa in the United States.

00:14:14.709 --> 00:14:18.839
But they didn’t find them in a field of
wheat or in a barn: they found them where

00:14:18.839 --> 00:14:22.380
you’d expect to find disease victims - a
hospital.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:26.160
More specifically, Foundation agents found
a number of corpses stuffed into the garbage

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:29.899
disposal units of the hospital of a small
Iowa town.

00:14:29.899 --> 00:14:33.990
The nurses and janitors at the hospital had
no idea what happened - they said that some

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:38.660
teenagers had broken in during the night and
dressed a number of scarecrows in scrubs before

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.170
leaving them in the wards as a prank.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:44.889
The staff in the morning had found and disposed
of them in the trash.

00:14:44.889 --> 00:14:50.509
Knowing what we know about SCP-2376, the actual
story is much more tragic.

00:14:50.509 --> 00:14:55.139
Somehow, the infection had probably gotten
into a human at the hospital, and the doctors

00:14:55.139 --> 00:14:58.040
began treating it the same as they would tetanus.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:03.070
The doctors and nurses had also gotten infected,
and quickly entered into Stage 2 while at

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.070
work.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:08.380
But remember - victims stop being perceived
as scarecrows when they die, which means that

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:13.889
when the hospital staff threw them into the
trash, they were still alive - if you can

00:15:13.889 --> 00:15:15.180
call that alive.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.420
But their thrashing and yelling couldn’t
be perceived by the others.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:22.910
Once they went into the disposal units, they
quickly deteriorated and died.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:25.889
A deeply tragic situation all around.

00:15:25.889 --> 00:15:29.180
But how did SCP-2376 get to the hospital?

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:31.089
Where did it even come from?

00:15:31.089 --> 00:15:33.880
Foundation agents have a pretty solid theory.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:38.750
They scoured the local town for any strange
events, incidents, or rumors about scarecrows,

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:41.730
and found something much bigger than what
they were expecting.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:46.079
A week before the corpses in the hospital
were discovered, a man in the next town over

00:15:46.079 --> 00:15:47.269
had died.

00:15:47.269 --> 00:15:49.709
Or more accurately - he had been killed.

00:15:49.709 --> 00:15:54.210
His wife called 911 incoherent and sobbing,
and explained to the operator that she had

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:58.690
found a spare scarecrow in the garage a week
before, and had nailed it up outside of the

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:00.579
house on a post.

00:16:00.579 --> 00:16:04.829
After three days, she had walked outside and
found, instead of the scarecrow, the body

00:16:04.829 --> 00:16:09.139
of her husband, at which point she broke down
and called 911.

00:16:09.139 --> 00:16:13.940
The woman was tried for murder but acquitted
on an insanity plea, based on her claims of

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:16.130
her husband having turned into a scarecrow.

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:20.540
The man’s corpse was sent to the morgue
at the hospital for an autopsy, which is probably

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.660
how the infection spread to other hospital
staff.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:28.980
But not before the autopsy was completed and
a report filed indicating cause of death:

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:33.029
dehydration from being out in the hot sun
for three days.

00:16:33.029 --> 00:16:37.980
Foundation staff quickly moved in and quarantined
the body, confirmed the presence of SCP-2376

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:43.470
in the blood and the wife confirmed her husband
had symptoms similar to tetanus a few weeks

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.470
ago.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:48.839
As for how the infection got into the man,
that remains a mystery.

00:16:48.839 --> 00:16:52.889
The outbreak was considered contained by the
Foundation, and since then there have been

00:16:52.889 --> 00:16:56.550
only cases here and there throughout the American
midwest.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:17:01.260
Until now - an addendum to the file indicates
that the Foundation has located and identified

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:07.550
a new strain of SCP-2376, the key difference
being the carrier and the effect.

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:13.160
Rather than crows, it is transmitted by pigeons
- and its origin point is in a highly urban

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:15.160
location in Illinois.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:20.030
More likely than not, it’s in the third
largest city in the United States - Chicago.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:24.550
And the second difference is that instead
of scarecrows, the infected are perceived

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:29.690
as inanimate mannequins, the kind you’d
see in any clothing or department store.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:33.940
Based off the vastly increased risk for an
epidemic, the Foundation’s medical department

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:38.890
have requested that SCP-2376 be reclassified
to Keter.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:44.360
SCP-2376 goes to show how even the diseases
we don’t know exist can be dangerous in

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.030
more ways than just threatening our lives.

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:51.590
So next time you see a crow scavenging for
food in your front lawn, maybe think twice

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.970
about getting too close to scare it away.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:18:00.000
You might just wind up on a pole in that same
front yard scaring crows away in your new

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.680
straw-stuffed overalls forever.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:09.000
Now go check out “SCP-1025 - Encyclopedia
of Common Diseases” and “SCP-610 - The

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:12.810
Flesh That Hates” for more on anomalous
diseases that will leave you crawling in your

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:12.840
skin!

